# NOT YET REPUBLISHED. `2026.07.14` carries neither cobra nor sksparse, so the
# curated-GEM lane cannot be built inside it and a missing CHOLMOD costs speed.
# `docker/ecspr/` builds what this name should resolve to -- both present, and
# asserted at build time -- but nothing is pushed yet, so the `conda:` key below
# is the working route (`dev/ecspr.sh --iecspr`).
#
# When it is pushed, repoint line 1 LAST, after the push, and re-stamp the
# method id: the container line is part of what the id hashes, so moving it
# ahead of the push names an image the registry does not have. The new tag is
# derived (`version.txt` + a content hash of src/ecspr) and can never collide
# with `2026.07.14` -- that digest must not move, or every artifact produced
# under it stops being reproducible.
container: docker://quay.io/hallamlab/ecspr:2026.07.14
conda: ecspr
